Technology

Technology shapes the world we live in, but its true power comes from the creativity,
responsibility, and vision of the people who use it.

Innovation and Creativity

“Any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic.”  
— Arthur C. Clarke

“Let’s go invent tomorrow instead of worrying about what happened yesterday.”  
— Steve Jobs

“Innovation is the outcome of a habit, not a random act.”  
— Sukant Ratnakar

“The great growling engine of change — technology.”  
— Alvin Toffler

“The tools of the future are being built by those willing to think beyond today.”  
— Naval Ravikant

Empowerment and Human Potential

“The number one benefit of information technology is that it empowers people to do what they want to do.”  
— Anonymous

“Technology is best when it brings people together.”  
— Matt Mullenweg

“Technology should improve your life… not become your life.”  
— Billy Cox

“The science of today is the technology of tomorrow.”  
— Edward Teller

“Technology is nothing. What’s important is that you have faith in people.”  
— Steve Jobs

Wisdom and Ethical Considerations

“If we continue to develop our technology without wisdom or prudence, our servant may prove to be our executioner.”  
— Omar N. Bradley

“Technology is a useful servant but a dangerous master.”  
— Christian Lous Lange

“The real problem is not whether machines think but whether men do.”  
— B. F. Skinner

“It has become appallingly obvious that our technology has exceeded our humanity.”  
— Albert Einstein

“We are stuck with technology when what we really want is just stuff that works.”  
— Douglas Adams

Insights on Learning and Adaptation

“The advance of technology is based on making it fit in so that you don’t really even notice it.”  
— Bill Gates

“Once a new technology rolls over you, if you’re not part of the steamroller, you’re part of the road.”  
— Stewart Brand

“Every great advance in science has issued from a new audacity of imagination.”  
— John Dewey

“Innovation distinguishes between a leader and a follower.”  
— Steve Jobs

“The next big thing is the one that makes the last big thing usable.”  
— Blake Ross

Reflection on Society and Technology

“Modern technology has become a total phenomenon for civilization, the defining force of a new social order.”  
— Jacques Ellul

“We are the children of a technological age. We have found streamlined ways of doing much of our routine work.”  
— Lawrence Clark Powell

“Technology forces us to live mythically.”  
— Marshall McLuhan

“In a world deluged by irrelevant information, clarity is power.”  
— Yuval Noah Harari
